    {
      "text": "Noah was a just man and perfect, Gen. 6:9 (Moses 8:27). walk before me, and be thou perfect, Gen. 17:1. Thou shalt be perfect with the Lord, Deut. 18:13. shalt have a perfect and just weight, Deut. 25:15. his work is perfect, Deut. 32:4. his way is perfect, 2 Sam. 22:31. Let your heart therefore be perfect with the Lord, 1 Kgs. 8:61. heart was not perfect with the Lord, 1 Kgs. 11:4 (15:3). house of the Lord was perfected, 2 Chr. 8:16. them whose heart is perfect toward him, 2 Chr. 16:9. Job … was perfect and upright, Job 1:1 (1:8). God, his way is perfect, Ps. 18:30. law of the Lord is perfect, Ps. 19:7. Zion, the perfection of beauty, Ps. 50:2. shineth … unto the perfect day, Prov. 4:18.",
